WEBVTT

1
00:00:49.042 --> 00:00:50.208
Fujimaki.

2
00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:53.500
Yes, Councilor Otomo?

3
00:00:53.583 --> 00:00:56.292
How do you assess this match?

4
00:00:56.375 --> 00:00:57.625
Well, uh…

5
00:01:01.833 --> 00:01:06.292
You will be checkmated
in seven moves, Councilor Otomo.

6
00:01:08.625 --> 00:01:11.208
I see! I'm losing, am I?

7
00:01:11.708 --> 00:01:13.875
By the way, Utayama.

8
00:01:13.958 --> 00:01:16.292
Last month's events were most unfortunate.

9
00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:19.833
Your late daughter kept
a tight command over the Ōoku.

10
00:01:20.333 --> 00:01:23.000
<i>It will be hard
to keep the maids in line without her.</i>

11
00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.708
<i>Not at all, sir!</i>

12
00:01:24.792 --> 00:01:28.708
My daughter can always be replaced.

13
00:01:28.792 --> 00:01:29.917
No.

14
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.792
It won't be easy.

15
00:01:32.417 --> 00:01:36.500
A castle crumbles
once its central pillar is lost.

16
00:01:36.583 --> 00:01:40.750
Such a castle is no place
for His Majesty to reside.

17
00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:42.958
The Utayama Family shall be abolished.

18
00:01:45.375 --> 00:01:47.958
P-Please reconsider, Councilor Otomo!

19
00:01:48.042 --> 00:01:51.625
Last month's disturbance
was the work of that wretched phantom!

20
00:01:51.708 --> 00:01:54.125
Even I couldn't foresee it!

21
00:01:54.208 --> 00:01:59.875
Preventing the unforeseeable
from occurring is your duty.

22
00:01:59.958 --> 00:02:01.167
Or rather,

23
00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:03.500
it <i>was </i>your duty.

24
00:02:04.292 --> 00:02:06.542
Careful now!

25
00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:08.500
Not too fast!

26
00:02:08.583 --> 00:02:10.958
Lower them slowly! Be gentle!

27
00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:15.083
Y-You're…

28
00:02:15.583 --> 00:02:17.875
Just a humble medicine seller.

29
00:02:18.625 --> 00:02:19.625
Here you are.

30
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.625
Thank you very much!

31
00:02:22.125 --> 00:02:23.542
Thank goodness.

32
00:02:23.625 --> 00:02:25.417
I was in for another scolding!

33
00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.542
It's because you insisted
on carrying them all at once, Kume.

34
00:02:28.625 --> 00:02:30.875
You agreed too, Tome!

35
00:02:30.958 --> 00:02:34.125
That's enough fighting, both of you.

36
00:02:34.208 --> 00:02:36.083
Repairing the lanterns already?

37
00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:37.167
Yes.

38
00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.875
The Ōoku has strict rules
about fire prevention.

39
00:02:40.958 --> 00:02:45.583
They say it's because
a woman burned to death long ago.

40
00:02:45.667 --> 00:02:46.542
Oh?

41
00:02:46.625 --> 00:02:49.083
Hey! Hold your tongue around outsiders!

42
00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:52.625
Huh? What's the big secret about that?

43
00:02:52.708 --> 00:02:55.042
I'll ask a professional to paper them.

44
00:02:55.125 --> 00:02:56.833
Return to your duties.

45
00:02:56.917 --> 00:02:58.208
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

46
00:03:01.208 --> 00:03:03.625
Why are you lurking around here again?

47
00:03:03.708 --> 00:03:06.875
You already got rid
of the <i>mononoke </i>last month!

48
00:03:06.958 --> 00:03:08.750
Indeed. One of them.

49
00:03:09.583 --> 00:03:10.583
One?

50
00:03:11.042 --> 00:03:12.500
<i>In this world,</i>

51
00:03:12.583 --> 00:03:15.125
<i>some passions linger,
even after they are slain.</i>

52
00:03:15.208 --> 00:03:16.583
What does that mean?

53
00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:18.333
Step right up, one and all!

54
00:03:18.417 --> 00:03:20.292
How about one of these?

55
00:03:20.375 --> 00:03:23.208
They're mouse talismans!

56
00:03:23.292 --> 00:03:25.542
They ensure fertility and safe childbirth.

57
00:03:25.625 --> 00:03:27.667
A foreign princess who bought one

58
00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:30.000
was blessed
with five sons and five daughters!

59
00:03:30.083 --> 00:03:31.083
Mice…

60
00:03:32.208 --> 00:03:33.208
You say?

61
00:03:38.125 --> 00:03:42.083
MONONOKE THE MOVIE:
CHAPTER II - THE ASHES OF RAGE

62
00:04:09.667 --> 00:04:13.458
- Look out for fire!
- Look out for fire!

63
00:04:16.083 --> 00:04:18.458
Oh, look! It's Lady Fuki.

64
00:04:18.542 --> 00:04:20.625
She's on her way to perform night work.

65
00:04:21.125 --> 00:04:22.958
She's so pretty!

66
00:04:23.042 --> 00:04:26.083
What do you expect
from His Majesty's nighttime companion?

67
00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:28.292
But it must be tough, right?

68
00:04:28.375 --> 00:04:30.875
The concubines summoned for night work

69
00:04:30.958 --> 00:04:33.458
all shoulder the fate of their family.

70
00:04:33.542 --> 00:04:34.375
Their family?

71
00:04:34.458 --> 00:04:36.000
Whoever bears a child

72
00:04:36.083 --> 00:04:38.875
will be the mother
of His Majesty's heir, right?

73
00:04:38.958 --> 00:04:41.292
Their family will
immediately rise to the top.

74
00:04:41.375 --> 00:04:43.000
Families, huh?

75
00:04:43.083 --> 00:04:44.083
Ahem.

76
00:04:44.458 --> 00:04:47.208
- Lady Botan!
- Lady Botan!

77
00:04:47.292 --> 00:04:48.958
Are you both resting at once?

78
00:04:49.042 --> 00:04:50.792
- No!
- We just…

79
00:04:50.875 --> 00:04:53.042
The Ōoku relies on the fire patrol.

80
00:04:53.125 --> 00:04:55.083
If you overlook a potential fire source,

81
00:04:55.167 --> 00:04:58.167
<i>His Majesty too
will be vulnerable to the blaze.</i>

82
00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:59.333
Understand?

83
00:04:59.417 --> 00:05:01.542
- We're sorry!
- We're sorry!

84
00:05:01.625 --> 00:05:03.792
Don't let it happen again.

85
00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:10.792
- Lady Botan is pretty too!
- Oh, you…

86
00:05:12.375 --> 00:05:14.417
How do you like that, Tokita?

87
00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:17.458
Oh, uh… What can I say?

88
00:05:17.542 --> 00:05:20.208
'Tis I, Councilor Fujimaki!
Forgive the intrusion.

89
00:05:21.625 --> 00:05:24.417
Councilor Otomo,
there is something we must discuss.

90
00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:26.292
What is it? Speak.

91
00:05:26.875 --> 00:05:29.292
It is not for the ears
of subordinates, sir.

92
00:05:29.375 --> 00:05:31.125
Pay him no mind.

93
00:05:31.208 --> 00:05:32.208
Now speak!

94
00:05:33.458 --> 00:05:34.292
Very well.

95
00:05:34.375 --> 00:05:38.708
It concerns the princess who was born
last month to His Majesty's consort.

96
00:05:38.792 --> 00:05:42.000
The time has come to appoint a guardian.

97
00:05:42.083 --> 00:05:45.417
The consort has indicated
she would like to raise the child herself.

98
00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:46.333
Unacceptable!

99
00:05:46.417 --> 00:05:50.125
A guardian should be chosen
from among the concubines.

100
00:05:50.208 --> 00:05:52.500
But the consort wishes...

101
00:05:52.583 --> 00:05:55.833
Lady Yukiko is not His Majesty.

102
00:05:55.917 --> 00:05:57.167
Of course, sir!

103
00:05:58.500 --> 00:05:59.375
In that case,

104
00:05:59.458 --> 00:06:01.875
<i>taking family names into consideration,</i>

105
00:06:01.958 --> 00:06:03.333
<i>perhaps Katsunuma would do.</i>

106
00:06:03.417 --> 00:06:05.667
<i>Oh! Katsunuma, eh?</i>

107
00:06:06.625 --> 00:06:08.500
You're quite perceptive.

108
00:06:09.083 --> 00:06:11.833
Very well! The Katsunuma Family it is.

109
00:06:13.167 --> 00:06:15.542
- It's your move.
- Right.

110
00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:19.000
Any thoughts on what you heard?

111
00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:22.708
Such important matters are the domain
of you esteemed councilors.

112
00:06:22.792 --> 00:06:23.625
I could never...

113
00:06:23.708 --> 00:06:27.625
Guardian selection can become a spark.

114
00:06:27.708 --> 00:06:29.000
A spark?

115
00:06:29.083 --> 00:06:31.167
If no male heir is born,

116
00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:33.458
the princess will marry

117
00:06:33.542 --> 00:06:35.750
and assume the role of the next consort.

118
00:06:35.833 --> 00:06:40.125
Her guardian will then become the mother
of His Majesty without giving birth.

119
00:06:40.208 --> 00:06:42.833
That gives her tremendous power.

120
00:06:44.125 --> 00:06:46.042
Left unattended,

121
00:06:46.125 --> 00:06:48.250
even the smallest spark becomes a blaze.

122
00:06:48.833 --> 00:06:50.000
The important thing

123
00:06:50.083 --> 00:06:54.250
is maintaining the ruling order
of the past 150 years.

124
00:06:54.333 --> 00:06:57.833
That will in turn protect His Majesty.

125
00:06:57.917 --> 00:07:00.542
You are right in every respect, sir.

126
00:07:00.625 --> 00:07:02.333
- That reminds me, Tokita.
- Yes?

127
00:07:02.417 --> 00:07:04.583
About your daughter…

128
00:07:04.667 --> 00:07:07.417
<i>Lady Fuki, wasn't it?</i>

129
00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:09.250
<i>That is correct, sir.</i>

130
00:07:09.333 --> 00:07:11.833
<i>She seems to receive</i>

131
00:07:11.917 --> 00:07:14.542
<i>great favor from His Majesty.</i>

132
00:07:14.625 --> 00:07:15.750
<i>Indeed.</i>

133
00:07:15.833 --> 00:07:17.208
<i>We are most grateful.</i>

134
00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:21.667
<i>Lady Fuki and Lady Botan
are both beautiful.</i>

135
00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:23.125
<i>But with that said,</i>

136
00:07:23.208 --> 00:07:25.792
<i>the one most likely
to give birth to the next heir</i>

137
00:07:25.875 --> 00:07:27.750
<i>is Lady Fuki from the Tokita Family.</i>

138
00:07:28.375 --> 00:07:31.542
<i>She enjoys His Majesty's exclusive favor.</i>

139
00:07:31.625 --> 00:07:33.292
<i>Are you sure?</i>

140
00:07:33.375 --> 00:07:35.708
<i>Lady Botan is from the Otomo Family.</i>

141
00:07:36.292 --> 00:07:38.667
<i>They hold great sway within the Ōoku,</i>

142
00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:42.667
<i>and most of all,
she's Councilor Otomo's daughter.</i>

143
00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:45.000
<i>Family names don't matter!</i>

144
00:07:45.083 --> 00:07:48.125
<i>No matter who the mother is,
the heir is the heir.</i>

145
00:07:48.625 --> 00:07:52.083
<i>Whether she's a merchant's daughter
or even a farmer's daughter,</i>

146
00:07:52.167 --> 00:07:53.917
she wins if she gives birth!

147
00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:57.333
Isn't that how the Ōoku works?

148
00:07:57.917 --> 00:08:02.042
My own daughter, Botan,
could learn a thing or two.

149
00:08:10.625 --> 00:08:11.458
Oh, my!

150
00:08:11.542 --> 00:08:13.500
Are you sure about that move?

151
00:08:14.208 --> 00:08:16.750
Checkmate in five moves!

152
00:08:16.833 --> 00:08:18.208
Astounding!

153
00:08:18.292 --> 00:08:21.542
As expected, I'm no match for you,
Councilor Otomo.

154
00:08:26.708 --> 00:08:29.125
Huh? Lord Tokita?

155
00:08:29.625 --> 00:08:31.125
I'd like to visit with my sister.

156
00:08:31.708 --> 00:08:34.792
I'll wait here until the appointed time.

157
00:08:34.875 --> 00:08:37.000
That won't be a problem.

158
00:08:44.167 --> 00:08:45.250
Is that okay?

159
00:08:45.333 --> 00:08:46.500
He had no pass.

160
00:08:46.583 --> 00:08:49.625
The Mizorogi family are an exception.

161
00:08:50.292 --> 00:08:53.583
Something about a special duty
to protect the Water Goddess.

162
00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:56.542
To be honest, we don't know the details.

163
00:08:56.625 --> 00:09:00.125
What an enviable position.

164
00:09:00.208 --> 00:09:01.208
Medicine Seller!

165
00:09:01.708 --> 00:09:03.917
Sneak in again, and it's your head!

166
00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:10.042
Oh, Tsuyu.

167
00:09:11.042 --> 00:09:12.208
So there you are.

168
00:09:12.917 --> 00:09:15.000
No wonder you didn't come when I called.

169
00:09:15.083 --> 00:09:16.792
Forgive me, my lady.

170
00:09:16.875 --> 00:09:20.333
They're shorthanded,
so I was asked to help.

171
00:09:20.417 --> 00:09:21.958
Oh, that's right.

172
00:09:22.042 --> 00:09:26.250
Lady Fuki, Madam Suikoin is inside.

173
00:09:26.833 --> 00:09:28.458
What are you worried about?

174
00:09:28.542 --> 00:09:30.958
<i>She's His Majesty's mother.</i>

175
00:09:31.042 --> 00:09:32.458
I'll handle myself.

176
00:09:32.958 --> 00:09:35.167
Then I guess I worried for nothing.

177
00:09:36.458 --> 00:09:38.333
Please go ahead.

178
00:09:38.417 --> 00:09:39.917
We'll speak later.

179
00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:47.792
Lady Fuki acts like
all the other concubines these days.

180
00:09:48.583 --> 00:09:49.583
Now, now…

181
00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:53.875
Only a year ago,
we were fetching water together.

182
00:09:53.958 --> 00:09:55.167
Sayo.

183
00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:57.833
<i>It's His Majesty
whose feelings have bloomed</i>

184
00:09:57.917 --> 00:09:59.292
<i>for Lady Fuki.</i>

185
00:10:03.667 --> 00:10:05.250
We therefore believe

186
00:10:05.333 --> 00:10:10.583
that Lady Matsu of the Katsunuma Family
will be a suitable guardian.

187
00:10:11.167 --> 00:10:14.083
I humbly ask for your acceptance.

188
00:10:16.583 --> 00:10:18.250
I am honored.

189
00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:21.583
But what about the consort?

190
00:10:21.667 --> 00:10:22.833
Right?

191
00:10:23.333 --> 00:10:25.458
The role of a princess's guardian

192
00:10:25.542 --> 00:10:29.875
has traditionally been given to a family
that has long served His Majesty.

193
00:10:29.958 --> 00:10:33.250
The Katsunuma Family is a fitting choice.

194
00:10:33.875 --> 00:10:35.750
You humble me with your words.

195
00:10:37.125 --> 00:10:39.917
May I ask one thing?

196
00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:44.583
What is to be made
of the consort's feelings?

197
00:10:45.083 --> 00:10:47.000
It's her first child after all.

198
00:10:47.083 --> 00:10:50.500
I imagine she probably wants
to raise the child herself.

199
00:10:50.583 --> 00:10:51.833
That's true.

200
00:10:51.917 --> 00:10:55.167
It's akin to kidnapping.

201
00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:58.750
I can only hope it doesn't bring her pain.

202
00:10:58.833 --> 00:11:00.375
Such impertinence!

203
00:11:00.458 --> 00:11:03.125
Are you saying you don't trust my family?

204
00:11:03.208 --> 00:11:04.917
I would never!

205
00:11:05.417 --> 00:11:08.917
I simply wonder
what the consort and His Majesty

206
00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:11.167
think about this.

207
00:11:12.042 --> 00:11:15.333
Parents can't help
but feel for their children.

208
00:11:16.333 --> 00:11:20.458
She's got some nerve saying that
after she stole His Majesty away!

209
00:11:20.542 --> 00:11:23.875
Anyway, what could
a poor draper's daughter know?

210
00:11:23.958 --> 00:11:25.875
Just because she's a bit attractive…

211
00:11:30.458 --> 00:11:32.167
<i>For that reason, I suggest</i>

212
00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:35.333
that we seek His Majesty's opinion.

213
00:11:35.917 --> 00:11:38.542
No matter how much
we debate among ourselves,

214
00:11:38.625 --> 00:11:40.542
some things are beyond our authority.

215
00:11:40.625 --> 00:11:43.083
That will not be necessary.

216
00:11:44.333 --> 00:11:47.625
His Majesty depends on us
to settle trivial matters

217
00:11:47.708 --> 00:11:50.792
so that he may focus on his duties.

218
00:11:50.875 --> 00:11:53.500
Is that not the role of the Ōoku?

219
00:11:54.458 --> 00:11:56.958
Bringing such a matter to his attention

220
00:11:57.042 --> 00:11:58.833
is out of the question.

221
00:11:58.917 --> 00:11:59.958
In that case,

222
00:12:00.042 --> 00:12:04.000
Lady Matsu shall be appointed guardian.

223
00:12:04.667 --> 00:12:06.875
Does anyone else wish to be heard?

224
00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:09.500
Moving on.

225
00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:12.583
Given the passing
of Madam Utayama last month,

226
00:12:12.667 --> 00:12:15.000
we must decide who will manage the Ōoku.

227
00:12:15.083 --> 00:12:17.833
The candidates proposed in advance are

228
00:12:18.417 --> 00:12:19.292
Lady Botan,

229
00:12:19.375 --> 00:12:20.583
Lady Matsu,

230
00:12:20.667 --> 00:12:23.583
and Lady Take.

231
00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:28.292
Of those candidates, Lady Botan
has long assisted Madam Utayama

232
00:12:28.375 --> 00:12:30.042
and has ties to various lords.

233
00:12:30.125 --> 00:12:32.542
We believe she is the best candidate.

234
00:12:33.042 --> 00:12:36.417
In that case, Lady Botan shall be
the next administrator of the Ōoku.

235
00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:38.917
I humbly ask for your acceptance.

236
00:12:39.417 --> 00:12:42.708
I humbly accept the responsibility.

237
00:12:50.458 --> 00:12:52.458
Since Madam Utayama's passing,

238
00:12:52.542 --> 00:12:56.583
I'm sure there are many
who are uncertain about the Ōoku's future.

239
00:12:56.667 --> 00:13:00.542
We must recommit to our duties
as maids of the Ōoku

240
00:13:01.208 --> 00:13:05.250
and devote ourselves to the rules
we are sworn to uphold.

241
00:13:06.083 --> 00:13:09.250
In particular, we must reaffirm
the rules governing night work,

242
00:13:09.333 --> 00:13:12.125
which have been neglected lately.

243
00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:16.000
The first rule

244
00:13:16.042 --> 00:13:20.792
is that conversation with His Majesty
during night work is forbidden.

245
00:13:20.875 --> 00:13:23.208
Written correspondence is also taboo.

246
00:13:24.125 --> 00:13:25.208
The second rule

247
00:13:25.292 --> 00:13:29.750
is that the consort and the concubines
shall alternate performing night work.

248
00:13:31.208 --> 00:13:34.958
No individual may perform night work
for two consecutive nights.

249
00:13:35.042 --> 00:13:36.542
Wait a minute!

250
00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:38.542
Yes?

251
00:13:39.042 --> 00:13:41.125
You're overstepping your bounds.

252
00:13:41.208 --> 00:13:44.333
His Majesty is the one who chooses
his night work companion.

253
00:13:44.833 --> 00:13:48.583
Not even the administrator
can interfere with that!

254
00:13:48.667 --> 00:13:52.667
The rule is in place
to ensure that an heir is born.

255
00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:55.417
It has always been deemed a taboo.

256
00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:56.500
But that's…

257
00:13:56.542 --> 00:13:59.583
What if His Majesty
bestowed favor on one woman

258
00:14:00.208 --> 00:14:02.708
and she could not bear children?

259
00:14:02.792 --> 00:14:05.292
His Majesty's bloodline would be lost.

260
00:14:06.583 --> 00:14:07.833
That may be,

261
00:14:07.917 --> 00:14:11.417
but you can't ignore His Majesty's will.

262
00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:15.125
Last night, the night before that,
and the night before that too,

263
00:14:15.208 --> 00:14:18.333
His Majesty chose me for night work.

264
00:14:18.417 --> 00:14:20.167
- What of it?
- Huh?

265
00:14:20.667 --> 00:14:23.917
Surely he hasn't told you
to return again the next night.

266
00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:28.000
After all, conversation is taboo
during night work.

267
00:14:28.083 --> 00:14:32.083
In the first place, it was His Majesty
who chose the new administrator.

268
00:14:32.167 --> 00:14:36.958
That means His Majesty
agrees with Lady Botan.

269
00:14:37.458 --> 00:14:39.292
Do you intend to defy that?

270
00:14:45.167 --> 00:14:47.208
What are you laughing at?!

271
00:14:47.292 --> 00:14:50.458
In the end, all you care about
is family names!

272
00:14:50.542 --> 00:14:53.542
You're merely jealous of the favor
His Majesty has bestowed on me!

273
00:14:53.625 --> 00:14:55.125
I only…

274
00:15:03.625 --> 00:15:05.042
Lady Fuki!

275
00:15:05.125 --> 00:15:07.500
Someone call for the court physician!

276
00:15:09.042 --> 00:15:10.417
GOLD COIN

277
00:15:14.333 --> 00:15:16.667
Doctor Gentaku! It's Lady Fuki!

278
00:15:24.292 --> 00:15:25.833
I didn't expect her to collapse.

279
00:15:25.917 --> 00:15:28.167
It must have been quite vexing for her.

280
00:15:29.250 --> 00:15:31.292
Lady Fuki's condition…

281
00:15:31.375 --> 00:15:33.792
Could it be morning sickness?

282
00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:35.542
That must be it!

283
00:15:35.625 --> 00:15:38.000
After all the favor from His Majesty…

284
00:15:38.083 --> 00:15:40.917
I'm sure His Majesty will be pleased!

285
00:15:41.667 --> 00:15:42.667
This is

286
00:15:43.583 --> 00:15:45.125
a dilemma.

287
00:15:47.083 --> 00:15:49.750
Indeed. It's not right.

288
00:15:51.333 --> 00:15:56.042
The thought of that vulgar woman
mixing with His Majesty's bloodline…

289
00:15:56.125 --> 00:15:57.125
Huh?

290
00:15:59.875 --> 00:16:01.917
It burns!

291
00:16:02.792 --> 00:16:04.417
Hey, what's happening?

292
00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:06.917
Is it… taking Form?

293
00:16:13.458 --> 00:16:14.583
It burns!

294
00:16:15.708 --> 00:16:17.042
Sayo?

295
00:16:19.625 --> 00:16:20.625
She's hot!

296
00:16:21.083 --> 00:16:22.458
My hand!

297
00:16:24.417 --> 00:16:25.417
Get them…

298
00:16:25.875 --> 00:16:26.875
Get them…

299
00:16:27.333 --> 00:16:31.750
Get them off of me!

300
00:16:31.833 --> 00:16:34.000
Halt! Where are you going?

301
00:16:34.083 --> 00:16:36.125
My pass is right here.

302
00:16:37.042 --> 00:16:40.250
That pass was given to you
by Madam Utayama!

303
00:16:40.333 --> 00:16:41.917
It's no longer valid!

304
00:16:49.375 --> 00:16:50.417
This one…

305
00:16:52.333 --> 00:16:53.792
Is fast!

306
00:16:57.375 --> 00:16:59.000
It burns!

307
00:17:31.917 --> 00:17:33.667
I am a guard of the Ōoku.

308
00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:35.958
I can't allow you
to enter without permission.

309
00:17:36.042 --> 00:17:39.500
It hides fast too.

310
00:17:41.208 --> 00:17:42.542
Silence!

311
00:17:46.417 --> 00:17:49.250
The men shall investigate this matter.

312
00:17:50.292 --> 00:17:52.542
You all must pry no further.

313
00:17:53.125 --> 00:17:54.625
Forget this ever happened.

314
00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:57.625
Don't you agree, Councilor Fujimaki?

315
00:17:58.542 --> 00:17:59.542
Yes!

316
00:18:02.875 --> 00:18:04.250
You scared me for nothing.

317
00:18:04.333 --> 00:18:05.333
No.

318
00:18:05.708 --> 00:18:07.833
The sparks are already…

319
00:18:07.917 --> 00:18:09.292
Master Tokita!

320
00:18:10.208 --> 00:18:13.083
Lady Fuki has fainted!

321
00:18:13.167 --> 00:18:14.167
My sister?

322
00:18:17.458 --> 00:18:18.708
Fuki!

323
00:18:18.792 --> 00:18:20.875
Oh, my. Hello there.

324
00:18:22.583 --> 00:18:25.000
There is no need to worry.

325
00:18:25.083 --> 00:18:26.958
She recovered her senses immediately.

326
00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:31.167
I haven't seen you
in a while either, Father.

327
00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:33.625
Oh, uh, that's true.

328
00:18:33.708 --> 00:18:36.167
I've heard whispers

329
00:18:36.667 --> 00:18:39.792
that you've been playing shogi
with Councilor Otomo.

330
00:18:39.875 --> 00:18:40.875
Oh, uh…

331
00:18:46.042 --> 00:18:48.167
You must rest for the time being.

332
00:18:50.208 --> 00:18:51.208
Father.

333
00:18:51.625 --> 00:18:52.917
Oh, right.

334
00:18:57.333 --> 00:18:58.500
Fuki,

335
00:18:59.083 --> 00:19:01.250
would it not be wise to leave the Ōoku?

336
00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:05.917
A concubine is bound for life.

337
00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:08.542
Leaving the Ōoku is not an option.

338
00:19:09.125 --> 00:19:12.792
After observing last month's events,
you surely understand that.

339
00:19:12.875 --> 00:19:14.625
But that's exactly why!

340
00:19:15.292 --> 00:19:17.042
I saw it with my own two eyes.

341
00:19:17.625 --> 00:19:19.208
The grudge haunting the Ōoku

342
00:19:19.292 --> 00:19:21.250
that curses all the maids to death!

343
00:19:22.083 --> 00:19:24.958
I'm worried about your safety!

344
00:19:25.458 --> 00:19:26.875
Aren't you, Father?

345
00:19:26.958 --> 00:19:28.958
Well, uh, yes.

346
00:19:29.042 --> 00:19:30.792
- And?
- Huh?

347
00:19:31.292 --> 00:19:32.542
If I flee from here,

348
00:19:33.125 --> 00:19:34.625
what happens then?

349
00:19:34.708 --> 00:19:37.375
Father's appointment as a samurai

350
00:19:37.458 --> 00:19:39.583
and your advancement in the ranks

351
00:19:39.667 --> 00:19:42.417
are both due to the favor
I receive from His Majesty.

352
00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:44.333
You want to give that up?

353
00:19:44.833 --> 00:19:48.083
Are you suggesting we starve
in that shabby row house again?

354
00:19:48.167 --> 00:19:49.458
That's…

355
00:19:49.542 --> 00:19:51.417
You too, Father.

356
00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:53.375
"The Tokita Family will gain power."

357
00:19:53.458 --> 00:19:55.583
"We will rule the land!"

358
00:19:55.667 --> 00:19:58.208
The one who sent me here to achieve that

359
00:19:58.292 --> 00:19:59.667
was you!

360
00:20:00.167 --> 00:20:02.167
If I turn tail and run now,

361
00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:04.333
why did I come here in the first place?

362
00:20:07.583 --> 00:20:08.958
Besides,

363
00:20:09.042 --> 00:20:11.417
our goal is truly within grasp.

364
00:20:11.958 --> 00:20:13.333
You don't mean…

365
00:20:13.417 --> 00:20:16.292
You no longer have anything to fear.

366
00:20:16.375 --> 00:20:18.875
Lady Fuki, are you pregnant?

367
00:20:22.208 --> 00:20:24.125
What? In the grand chamber?

368
00:20:24.208 --> 00:20:26.958
We've been ordered to investigate.

369
00:20:28.458 --> 00:20:29.750
What is it?

370
00:20:29.833 --> 00:20:31.542
Oh, it's nothing.

371
00:20:31.625 --> 00:20:32.625
Forget it.

372
00:20:32.708 --> 00:20:35.292
Hey! Where did he go?

373
00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:39.500
My, my.

374
00:20:39.583 --> 00:20:41.250
This is quite a development.

375
00:20:41.333 --> 00:20:43.583
To think someone would burn in the Ōoku.

376
00:20:43.667 --> 00:20:46.417
There's that too,
but the bigger problem is…

377
00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:50.042
Do you mean Tokita's daughter Fuki?

378
00:20:50.125 --> 00:20:51.125
Indeed.

379
00:20:51.208 --> 00:20:53.500
If she happens to give birth to a boy,

380
00:20:53.583 --> 00:20:56.083
<i>conflict over succession is inevitable.</i>

381
00:20:56.167 --> 00:21:00.292
Since the Katsunuma Family relies
on being the princess's guardian,

382
00:21:00.375 --> 00:21:02.542
your position will also be threatened.

383
00:21:02.625 --> 00:21:03.625
Perhaps.

384
00:21:04.083 --> 00:21:10.042
But surely no one would accept
the child of a draper's daughter as heir.

385
00:21:10.125 --> 00:21:11.750
- It's the opposite.
- What?

386
00:21:11.833 --> 00:21:16.292
She'll receive support from those
dissatisfied with the ruling order.

387
00:21:16.375 --> 00:21:17.792
<i>That girl</i>

388
00:21:17.875 --> 00:21:20.208
<i>has become a spark!</i>

389
00:21:20.292 --> 00:21:21.417
I see.

390
00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:24.875
Perhaps we should consult Councilor Otomo.

391
00:21:24.958 --> 00:21:26.958
He must not hear of this!

392
00:21:27.042 --> 00:21:30.208
Fuki giving birth is something

393
00:21:30.292 --> 00:21:31.667
he hasn't foreseen.

394
00:21:32.583 --> 00:21:35.417
Remember what happened to Utayama?

395
00:21:36.083 --> 00:21:40.292
Fires that begin within the Ōoku
must be extinguished within the Ōoku!

396
00:21:40.375 --> 00:21:42.125
Left unattended,

397
00:21:42.208 --> 00:21:44.958
even the smallest spark becomes a blaze.

398
00:21:45.042 --> 00:21:49.542
In that case, let us leave this matter
to my daughter Matsu.

399
00:21:49.625 --> 00:21:52.375
<i>We must not aggravate things further.</i>

400
00:21:52.458 --> 00:21:53.958
<i>Handle it quietly.</i>

401
00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:02.583
Have you faced any difficulties
since Madam Utayama's passing?

402
00:22:03.208 --> 00:22:05.083
A young official scribe such as yourself

403
00:22:05.167 --> 00:22:07.583
must be a target of envy.

404
00:22:08.375 --> 00:22:09.667
If you're ever in need,

405
00:22:09.750 --> 00:22:12.500
you may approach me at any time.

406
00:22:12.583 --> 00:22:13.958
<i>By asking my father,</i>

407
00:22:14.042 --> 00:22:16.292
most things can be arranged.

408
00:22:21.333 --> 00:22:23.792
You humble me with your concern,

409
00:22:23.875 --> 00:22:26.750
but my duties keep me occupied.

410
00:22:26.833 --> 00:22:28.500
I have no time to worry.

411
00:22:31.208 --> 00:22:32.208
The important thing

412
00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:36.708
<i>is maintaining the ruling order
of the past 150 years.</i>

413
00:22:37.708 --> 00:22:41.208
<i>That and service to His Majesty.</i>

414
00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:46.083
Don't ever forget that mindset.

415
00:22:48.458 --> 00:22:49.625
Understood.

416
00:22:51.417 --> 00:22:52.708
Choju.

417
00:22:53.292 --> 00:22:56.167
I assume you haven't forgotten

418
00:22:56.250 --> 00:22:58.042
the day you were appointed Matron.

419
00:22:58.125 --> 00:23:01.250
It is only due
to the Katsunuma Family's endorsement

420
00:23:01.333 --> 00:23:04.458
that I am able to spend my days
serving His Majesty.

421
00:23:05.542 --> 00:23:06.708
Take this.

422
00:23:07.500 --> 00:23:09.125
To the night chamber.

423
00:23:10.500 --> 00:23:12.792
As you wish.

424
00:23:20.250 --> 00:23:22.083
Hey! You creep!

425
00:23:22.167 --> 00:23:23.625
I finally found you!

426
00:23:24.708 --> 00:23:26.500
Men aren't allowed in the Ōoku!

427
00:23:26.583 --> 00:23:28.458
Do you want to lose your head?

428
00:23:29.375 --> 00:23:30.375
Hey!

429
00:23:31.250 --> 00:23:33.583
Someone has burned.

430
00:23:34.833 --> 00:23:37.000
Where did you hear that?

431
00:23:39.333 --> 00:23:40.833
I can tell by sight.

432
00:23:40.917 --> 00:23:43.375
There is a <i>mononoke </i>present.

433
00:23:44.417 --> 00:23:46.833
A passion that burns humans alive,

434
00:23:46.917 --> 00:23:49.542
turning even their bones
and marrow to ashes.

435
00:23:51.208 --> 00:23:53.083
You have an idea what it may be.

436
00:23:53.167 --> 00:23:54.500
Don't you?

437
00:23:56.125 --> 00:23:58.208
Don't be ridiculous!

438
00:23:58.292 --> 00:24:01.292
Just get out of here
before there's trouble!

439
00:24:02.708 --> 00:24:05.667
You leave me no choice.

440
00:24:06.333 --> 00:24:08.792
It will return tonight.

441
00:24:09.792 --> 00:24:10.792
What?

442
00:24:11.958 --> 00:24:14.833
Beware… of fire.

443
00:24:19.833 --> 00:24:20.833
A <i>mononoke</i>?

444
00:24:21.417 --> 00:24:24.542
Some are saying
it's a curse left by Lady Suzu.

445
00:24:25.333 --> 00:24:27.833
How can a guard of the Ōoku

446
00:24:27.917 --> 00:24:31.125
tremble at such nonsense?

447
00:24:41.833 --> 00:24:45.083
If Lady Fuki gives birth to the heir,

448
00:24:45.167 --> 00:24:49.208
Lady Matsu's appointment as guardian
will have been for nothing.

449
00:24:50.542 --> 00:24:51.833
Okay!

450
00:24:52.625 --> 00:24:53.625
What is it?

451
00:24:54.292 --> 00:24:56.375
I need to check something.

452
00:24:56.875 --> 00:24:58.000
I'll be on patrol.

453
00:24:58.083 --> 00:24:59.708
Then I'll join you!

454
00:24:59.792 --> 00:25:02.125
It's fine. I'll be right back.

455
00:25:02.625 --> 00:25:05.875
I'm simply going to check for mice.

456
00:25:40.208 --> 00:25:41.333
Lady Fuki?

457
00:25:43.125 --> 00:25:44.417
Do you need water?

458
00:25:47.458 --> 00:25:48.542
Oh?

459
00:25:52.583 --> 00:25:55.917
- Look out for fire!
- Look out for fire!

460
00:26:20.958 --> 00:26:22.125
Ow, ow!

461
00:26:30.708 --> 00:26:35.083
It burns!

462
00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:42.333
It's nearby.

463
00:26:46.958 --> 00:26:48.042
It burns!

464
00:26:51.750 --> 00:26:53.875
It burns!

465
00:26:54.542 --> 00:26:56.083
- Tome, look!
- Oh, no!

466
00:26:57.917 --> 00:26:59.583
It burns…

467
00:27:06.667 --> 00:27:07.792
It burns…

468
00:27:15.458 --> 00:27:17.542
It burns!

469
00:27:17.625 --> 00:27:20.667
Someone! Come quick!

470
00:27:30.958 --> 00:27:32.792
My flesh is seared!

471
00:27:34.125 --> 00:27:36.917
It burns!

472
00:27:38.708 --> 00:27:40.333
Are you okay?

473
00:27:41.042 --> 00:27:42.375
- She's hot!
- She's hot!

474
00:27:42.458 --> 00:27:43.792
- Get back!
- Medicine Seller!

475
00:27:47.458 --> 00:27:48.833
What's going on?

476
00:28:02.125 --> 00:28:04.125
We're surrounded.

477
00:28:11.833 --> 00:28:12.833
This is…

478
00:28:27.042 --> 00:28:28.208
What was that?

479
00:28:28.708 --> 00:28:30.542
Flames that move in swarms.

480
00:28:33.458 --> 00:28:34.833
This is the work of

481
00:28:35.583 --> 00:28:36.958
Hinezumi.

482
00:28:43.458 --> 00:28:45.250
I have identified… its Form.

483
00:28:47.542 --> 00:28:49.333
Another <i>mononoke</i>?

484
00:28:49.417 --> 00:28:50.417
Mere embers.

485
00:28:50.500 --> 00:28:51.500
Embers?

486
00:28:51.583 --> 00:28:55.667
The phantoms just now
were Hinezumi children.

487
00:28:57.792 --> 00:29:00.333
Their mother is elsewhere.

488
00:29:03.000 --> 00:29:08.750
Are you the suspicious man who was
reported in the Ōoku this afternoon?

489
00:29:09.375 --> 00:29:12.333
Hinezumi is an <i>ayakashi </i>who won't stop

490
00:29:12.417 --> 00:29:14.458
until it burns everything to ashes.

491
00:29:14.542 --> 00:29:15.917
Hinezumi?

492
00:29:16.000 --> 00:29:18.042
No matter what the situation,

493
00:29:18.125 --> 00:29:21.000
men can never enter the Ōoku.

494
00:29:21.500 --> 00:29:24.500
If we allow men in this easily,

495
00:29:24.583 --> 00:29:26.583
the Ōoku's rules are mere words.

496
00:29:27.083 --> 00:29:29.417
If we don't slay the source of the fire,

497
00:29:29.500 --> 00:29:31.000
before long…

498
00:29:31.083 --> 00:29:33.875
- Did you hear me?
- The Ōoku will go up in flames.

499
00:29:34.542 --> 00:29:36.417
However, the weapons you carry

500
00:29:36.500 --> 00:29:38.417
will be of no use.

501
00:29:39.625 --> 00:29:41.708
A <i>mononoke </i>can only be slain

502
00:29:41.792 --> 00:29:43.917
with this Sacred Sword.

503
00:29:45.542 --> 00:29:48.333
Then we shall borrow it from you.

504
00:29:48.833 --> 00:29:49.667
- Sakashita.
- Right!

505
00:29:49.750 --> 00:29:54.083
Unfortunately for you,
only we can wield the sword.

506
00:29:56.125 --> 00:29:59.375
Drawing it requires certain conditions.

507
00:29:59.875 --> 00:30:03.458
- Form, Truth, and Reason.
- This thing's h-heavy!

508
00:30:03.542 --> 00:30:06.833
Present those three elements,
and the sword can be drawn.

509
00:30:06.917 --> 00:30:09.250
Then the <i>mononoke </i>can be slain.

510
00:30:11.042 --> 00:30:13.208
Truth is the way things appear.

511
00:30:13.292 --> 00:30:15.667
Reason is that which smolders in the Ōoku.

512
00:30:15.750 --> 00:30:18.958
The true nature of the passions
that burn people to ashes.

513
00:30:19.458 --> 00:30:21.250
Therefore, ladies and gentlemen,

514
00:30:21.333 --> 00:30:22.708
I hereby request

515
00:30:22.792 --> 00:30:26.542
that you tell me everything.

516
00:30:26.625 --> 00:30:28.875
Passions that burn people to ashes?

517
00:30:30.500 --> 00:30:33.375
Palace guards, seize him at once!

518
00:30:34.500 --> 00:30:35.750
Lady Botan!

519
00:30:35.833 --> 00:30:38.708
This man was carrying a pass.

520
00:30:38.792 --> 00:30:41.667
That is why I let him through.

521
00:30:41.750 --> 00:30:43.625
Huh? Wait a minute!

522
00:30:43.708 --> 00:30:46.667
This is the pass he received
from Madam Utayama

523
00:30:46.750 --> 00:30:49.458
when he slew the <i>mononoke </i>last month!

524
00:30:49.958 --> 00:30:52.250
He can't use this now.

525
00:30:52.750 --> 00:30:54.625
What a rascal!

526
00:30:54.708 --> 00:30:57.542
Lady Botan,
please settle this one peacefully.

527
00:30:58.167 --> 00:31:02.500
After all, this man did save
the Ōoku once!

528
00:31:07.292 --> 00:31:09.875
For the crime
of mistakenly letting him pass,

529
00:31:10.375 --> 00:31:11.833
I will forgive you this once.

530
00:31:12.333 --> 00:31:14.417
However, I won't do so again.

531
00:31:14.500 --> 00:31:17.250
I am grateful for your mercy.

532
00:31:18.042 --> 00:31:19.917
Be thankful to Sakashita.

533
00:31:20.000 --> 00:31:21.167
Furthermore,

534
00:31:21.250 --> 00:31:23.417
never show your face here again.

535
00:31:23.500 --> 00:31:24.500
Oh?

536
00:31:30.875 --> 00:31:34.708
Thank you very much for your help.

537
00:31:34.792 --> 00:31:37.583
I merely happened to be passing by.

538
00:31:38.542 --> 00:31:39.708
You've got that right.

539
00:31:39.792 --> 00:31:42.167
Where did you even sneak in from?

540
00:31:42.250 --> 00:31:44.208
That was a surprise.

541
00:31:44.292 --> 00:31:47.500
I didn't think you'd cover
for the Medicine Seller, Master Sakashita.

542
00:31:47.583 --> 00:31:49.458
Don't get the wrong idea!

543
00:31:49.542 --> 00:31:52.667
I just figured we'll need
his skills to slay the <i>mononoke</i>.

544
00:31:53.667 --> 00:31:58.792
And yet, Lady Botan told me
never to show my face here again.

545
00:31:59.292 --> 00:32:01.417
She is still young.

546
00:32:02.000 --> 00:32:04.583
She's not accustomed to these things.

547
00:32:04.667 --> 00:32:07.000
Accustomed… to what things?

548
00:32:07.500 --> 00:32:09.417
Crises involving fire.

549
00:32:09.500 --> 00:32:10.625
Oh?

550
00:32:10.708 --> 00:32:13.750
No fire starts in the Ōoku by chance.

551
00:32:13.833 --> 00:32:15.458
Be it humans

552
00:32:15.542 --> 00:32:17.083
or <i>mononoke,</i>

553
00:32:17.167 --> 00:32:19.583
there is always a cause.

554
00:32:20.667 --> 00:32:21.917
As I suspected,

555
00:32:22.000 --> 00:32:24.500
you know what this is about.

556
00:32:24.583 --> 00:32:25.750
Well…

557
00:32:25.833 --> 00:32:27.667
Master Sakashita!

558
00:32:27.750 --> 00:32:31.708
It merely brought back memories
of what happened to Lady Suzu.

559
00:32:31.792 --> 00:32:34.000
Huh? Lady Suzu?

560
00:32:34.583 --> 00:32:37.583
<i>You mean the ghost in the grand chamber?</i>

561
00:32:37.667 --> 00:32:38.750
Ghost?

562
00:32:39.250 --> 00:32:42.208
Everyone on fire patrol knows about it.

563
00:32:42.292 --> 00:32:44.125
When we patrol at night,

564
00:32:44.208 --> 00:32:47.458
people often see a woman
with a lamp in the grand chamber.

565
00:32:47.958 --> 00:32:49.125
She's no ghost!

566
00:32:49.625 --> 00:32:54.292
Lady Suzu was a concubine 20 years ago.

567
00:32:55.833 --> 00:32:58.458
<i>She became pregnant,
but it didn't go well,</i>

568
00:32:58.958 --> 00:33:01.750
and one day she perished in a fire.

569
00:33:02.625 --> 00:33:03.458
A fire?

570
00:33:03.542 --> 00:33:06.708
Fortunately, the fire did not spread,

571
00:33:07.958 --> 00:33:11.583
but Lady Suzu fell victim,
by chance, to the flames.

572
00:33:12.208 --> 00:33:13.333
It happened

573
00:33:13.833 --> 00:33:15.792
in the grand chamber.

574
00:33:16.292 --> 00:33:19.000
The last person to see Lady Suzu…

575
00:33:22.542 --> 00:33:23.875
Was me.

576
00:33:25.333 --> 00:33:27.875
<i>If I had called out to her at that moment…</i>

577
00:33:28.917 --> 00:33:32.542
However, Lady Suzu was kindhearted.

578
00:33:32.625 --> 00:33:34.917
<i>She would never become a </i>mononoke

579
00:33:35.000 --> 00:33:36.625
<i>that kills others.</i>

580
00:33:36.708 --> 00:33:39.667
<i>At times, such kindness</i>

581
00:33:40.292 --> 00:33:42.667
can become a curse.

582
00:33:42.750 --> 00:33:43.917
What?

583
00:33:44.000 --> 00:33:47.500
<i>Mononoke </i>too possess Truth and Reason.

584
00:33:47.583 --> 00:33:49.333
Their feelings have a source.

585
00:33:49.417 --> 00:33:52.417
Hinezumi was originally
a guardian mouse deity.

586
00:33:53.375 --> 00:33:54.417
<i>It resides</i>

587
00:33:54.500 --> 00:33:57.417
<i>wherever parents wish for safe childbirth.</i>

588
00:33:58.458 --> 00:33:59.917
Medicine Seller,

589
00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:02.458
where is the <i>mononoke </i>now?

590
00:34:02.542 --> 00:34:04.167
Though it may go unseen,

591
00:34:04.250 --> 00:34:05.917
it is somewhere in the Ōoku.

592
00:34:06.000 --> 00:34:10.958
Which is why I have
a favor to ask of the two of you.

593
00:34:13.958 --> 00:34:16.208
<i>All manner of misfortune</i>

594
00:34:16.292 --> 00:34:18.167
- Now's our chance.
- Yeah.

595
00:34:20.708 --> 00:34:23.708
Hey! I'm busy, you know.

596
00:34:30.458 --> 00:34:31.500
Tsuyu?

597
00:34:32.792 --> 00:34:34.500
Is something wrong?

598
00:34:36.000 --> 00:34:36.833
<i>Choju?</i>

599
00:34:36.917 --> 00:34:38.708
<i>Rumor has it</i>

600
00:34:38.792 --> 00:34:40.875
<i>that it was the work of a </i>mononoke.

601
00:34:40.958 --> 00:34:41.958
Th-This is…

602
00:34:42.958 --> 00:34:44.083
A <i>mononoke</i>…

603
00:34:44.583 --> 00:34:46.792
It's merely a rumor.

604
00:34:47.292 --> 00:34:48.583
Thank you.

605
00:34:51.958 --> 00:34:54.917
This water… is tastier than usual.

606
00:34:55.417 --> 00:34:58.292
It was freshly drawn this morning.

607
00:35:01.625 --> 00:35:05.042
May I ask one thing?

608
00:35:05.125 --> 00:35:07.167
Oh? What is it?

609
00:35:07.250 --> 00:35:11.083
Why is it that you call for me
as your opponent, Councilor Otomo?

610
00:35:11.167 --> 00:35:13.208
Does playing shogi bore you?

611
00:35:13.292 --> 00:35:14.958
No! Not at all.

612
00:35:15.042 --> 00:35:18.333
Every piece has its role.

613
00:35:18.833 --> 00:35:20.958
Although they can be promoted,

614
00:35:21.042 --> 00:35:23.708
a pawn can never become a rook.

615
00:35:24.208 --> 00:35:27.208
Nor can a rook ever betray the king.

616
00:35:27.708 --> 00:35:29.333
In the game of shogi,

617
00:35:29.417 --> 00:35:32.750
there are no foolish subordinates,
nor scheming lords,

618
00:35:32.833 --> 00:35:35.917
nor fires that undo
all that has come before.

619
00:35:36.417 --> 00:35:38.542
And that's why I love it!

620
00:35:39.542 --> 00:35:42.458
These are leftovers.

621
00:35:43.042 --> 00:35:44.583
You've done enough.

622
00:35:44.667 --> 00:35:46.917
I appreciate your help.

623
00:35:47.000 --> 00:35:48.500
Not at all.

624
00:35:49.708 --> 00:35:51.750
You're on your own this time!

625
00:35:55.083 --> 00:35:59.583
<i>Purify</i>

626
00:36:00.542 --> 00:36:04.292
<i>Cleanse</i>

627
00:36:05.167 --> 00:36:06.708
Will you not drink?

628
00:36:06.792 --> 00:36:10.917
<i>By the will of heaven</i>

629
00:36:11.000 --> 00:36:14.458
- This was in Madam Utayama's room.
<i>- Protect us</i>

630
00:36:14.542 --> 00:36:16.375
At the spot where Choju died.

631
00:36:16.458 --> 00:36:17.500
What is it?

632
00:36:17.583 --> 00:36:20.875
It likely contained poison.

633
00:36:20.958 --> 00:36:24.833
When I gave some to the goldfish,
they died immediately.

634
00:36:24.917 --> 00:36:25.917
But…

635
00:36:26.000 --> 00:36:28.500
Wasn't Choju killed by a <i>mononoke</i>?

636
00:36:29.125 --> 00:36:30.917
You need not concern yourself

637
00:36:31.000 --> 00:36:33.917
with why Choju died.

638
00:36:34.000 --> 00:36:35.375
After all,

639
00:36:35.458 --> 00:36:37.917
it was you she intended to poison.

640
00:36:38.417 --> 00:36:40.417
What are you saying?

641
00:36:40.500 --> 00:36:45.750
A witness saw Choju
approaching your room last night.

642
00:36:45.833 --> 00:36:46.958
But that's…

643
00:36:47.542 --> 00:36:50.042
Did you bring me here to mock me then?

644
00:36:50.125 --> 00:36:53.583
It's that trait of yours that I dislike.

645
00:36:54.542 --> 00:36:55.917
No matter who the mother is,

646
00:36:56.000 --> 00:36:57.542
the heir is the heir.

647
00:36:58.458 --> 00:37:01.208
As the Ōoku's administrator,

648
00:37:01.292 --> 00:37:03.167
I have a duty to defend them.

649
00:37:03.250 --> 00:37:05.292
That's why I've given you this warning.

650
00:37:06.500 --> 00:37:09.000
But you fail to understand

651
00:37:09.083 --> 00:37:11.833
because you only think of yourself.

652
00:37:12.417 --> 00:37:16.500
You've never given any thought
to the future of the Ōoku.

653
00:37:16.583 --> 00:37:18.292
For you, an heir

654
00:37:18.375 --> 00:37:21.125
is merely a tool
for advancement, is it not?

655
00:37:23.917 --> 00:37:27.583
The one who remains bitter
over never being called for night work

656
00:37:27.667 --> 00:37:29.792
is you, is it not?

657
00:37:31.000 --> 00:37:32.750
Does that satisfy you?

658
00:37:36.750 --> 00:37:42.042
These scales will tell us
the <i>mononoke</i>'s location?

659
00:37:42.542 --> 00:37:44.583
Though it may go unseen…

660
00:37:47.000 --> 00:37:49.458
This sound will be our guide.

661
00:37:49.542 --> 00:37:51.042
How mysterious!

662
00:37:51.125 --> 00:37:52.125
So?

663
00:37:52.958 --> 00:37:56.958
You still haven't found
the Hinezumi thing, have you?

664
00:37:57.542 --> 00:37:59.083
Unless the <i>mononoke </i>makes a move,

665
00:37:59.708 --> 00:38:01.417
the scales will not ring.

666
00:38:03.250 --> 00:38:04.500
Unforgivable…

667
00:38:05.458 --> 00:38:08.708
Why?

668
00:38:08.792 --> 00:38:09.917
That child…

669
00:38:16.208 --> 00:38:17.625
"That child"?

670
00:38:20.333 --> 00:38:21.708
Hey, look!

671
00:38:22.667 --> 00:38:25.625
Once a deep-seated grudge is lit ablaze,

672
00:38:25.708 --> 00:38:28.583
it will not subside on its own.

673
00:38:32.583 --> 00:38:33.667
It's here.

674
00:38:33.750 --> 00:38:34.750
What?!

675
00:38:38.958 --> 00:38:40.000
Damn it all!

676
00:38:40.083 --> 00:38:41.833
Go do your thing!

677
00:38:41.917 --> 00:38:44.083
Medicine Seller!

678
00:38:48.750 --> 00:38:49.917
Take over for me.

679
00:38:50.000 --> 00:38:51.000
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

680
00:38:59.875 --> 00:39:01.625
This miraculous elixir

681
00:39:02.500 --> 00:39:06.750
has been passed down
by generations of court physicians.

682
00:39:12.125 --> 00:39:14.625
- Now then…
- Doctor Gentaku!

683
00:39:26.417 --> 00:39:29.042
Please pardon the intrusion.

684
00:39:29.750 --> 00:39:31.000
It burns!

685
00:39:35.125 --> 00:39:36.792
Unforgivable.

686
00:39:36.875 --> 00:39:37.708
Lady Suzu?

687
00:39:37.792 --> 00:39:40.458
- Where is your mother?
- What's happening?!

688
00:39:40.542 --> 00:39:43.750
I was hoping… you could tell me!

689
00:39:43.833 --> 00:39:45.792
Is Lady Fuki safe?

690
00:39:46.292 --> 00:39:47.917
Unforgivable!

691
00:39:49.583 --> 00:39:51.583
Why do I hear Lady Suzu's voice?

692
00:39:52.083 --> 00:39:53.083
This is…

693
00:39:55.708 --> 00:39:56.958
What's going on?

694
00:39:57.042 --> 00:39:58.042
Stay back!

695
00:39:58.417 --> 00:40:02.458
Doctor Gentaku tried to poison Lady Fuki!

696
00:40:03.333 --> 00:40:05.583
Y-You're wrong!

697
00:40:05.667 --> 00:40:08.708
- What did you do to the <i>mononoke</i>?!
- Forgive me!

698
00:40:08.792 --> 00:40:09.958
Master Sakashita!

699
00:40:10.042 --> 00:40:13.250
Unwanted children
have existed in every era!

700
00:40:14.583 --> 00:40:16.500
I merely did as I was ordered!

701
00:40:16.583 --> 00:40:17.458
Ordered by whom?

702
00:40:17.542 --> 00:40:19.875
The sparks of conflict
must be extinguished!

703
00:40:21.250 --> 00:40:22.542
Don't tell me…

704
00:40:22.625 --> 00:40:26.167
For generations,
that has been the court physician's duty!

705
00:40:26.250 --> 00:40:27.875
For generations?

706
00:40:27.958 --> 00:40:30.792
Did you abort Lady Suzu's
unborn child too?

707
00:40:31.583 --> 00:40:33.625
I merely prepared the potion!

708
00:40:33.708 --> 00:40:35.875
- You bastard!
- How could you?

709
00:40:37.250 --> 00:40:39.167
Lady Suzu!

710
00:40:40.042 --> 00:40:41.625
Unforgivable.

711
00:40:41.708 --> 00:40:44.167
Lady Suzu was a kind soul.

712
00:40:44.250 --> 00:40:45.750
It hurts!

713
00:40:48.417 --> 00:40:49.792
But you…

714
00:40:52.042 --> 00:40:55.250
You all… don't know either?

715
00:40:56.875 --> 00:40:57.875
You stole

716
00:40:58.417 --> 00:41:02.333
her child from her!

717
00:41:05.833 --> 00:41:07.917
I have identified… its Truth.

718
00:41:18.375 --> 00:41:19.375
What?

719
00:41:20.542 --> 00:41:21.542
It can't be!

720
00:41:29.333 --> 00:41:30.958
Lady Fuki!

721
00:41:32.542 --> 00:41:34.917
So that's it.

722
00:41:41.792 --> 00:41:43.333
The rules don't matter…

723
00:41:43.417 --> 00:41:45.917
- …when it comes to <i>mononoke</i>?
- She's hot to the touch.

724
00:41:46.000 --> 00:41:48.792
And you call yourself a palace guard?

725
00:41:48.875 --> 00:41:51.750
The only one who can save
the Ōoku from the <i>mononoke</i>

726
00:41:51.833 --> 00:41:53.167
is him, my lady.

727
00:41:54.208 --> 00:41:56.708
And so I should allow him to trespass?

728
00:41:57.208 --> 00:42:00.333
As long as the <i>mononoke</i>
possesses Lady Fuki's body,

729
00:42:00.917 --> 00:42:03.167
we cannot stand by.

730
00:42:05.500 --> 00:42:06.708
No matter when or how far,

731
00:42:07.500 --> 00:42:10.375
we have traveled
to where <i>mononoke </i>have appeared

732
00:42:10.458 --> 00:42:11.750
and slayed them.

733
00:42:12.250 --> 00:42:16.458
That is the fate of those of us
who carry the Sacred Sword.

734
00:42:17.542 --> 00:42:19.500
I have guarded the Nanatsu Gate

735
00:42:19.583 --> 00:42:21.042
for 30 years now.

736
00:42:21.542 --> 00:42:23.875
I, Sakashita, care only

737
00:42:23.958 --> 00:42:26.458
about protecting the Ōoku!

738
00:42:26.958 --> 00:42:28.250
Silence, Sakashita!

739
00:42:28.333 --> 00:42:31.708
Please! Heed my words of experience.

740
00:42:31.792 --> 00:42:34.125
I beg you!

741
00:42:34.208 --> 00:42:37.208
Will you lend me your ears?

742
00:42:38.625 --> 00:42:40.667
Once I have its Reason,

743
00:42:41.250 --> 00:42:43.500
I can draw my sword.

744
00:42:44.583 --> 00:42:45.583
Save Lady Fuki

745
00:42:46.375 --> 00:42:48.458
and the child she carries.

746
00:42:48.542 --> 00:42:50.167
Your punishment is on hold.

747
00:42:50.250 --> 00:42:51.250
Lady Botan!

748
00:42:52.250 --> 00:42:53.083
In that case,

749
00:42:53.167 --> 00:42:55.042
I have a favor to ask

750
00:42:55.542 --> 00:42:58.083
of all the Ōoku residents.

751
00:43:02.500 --> 00:43:04.000
I gathered as many as I could.

752
00:43:04.083 --> 00:43:05.958
You have done well.

753
00:43:07.292 --> 00:43:10.375
Why do you need all these mouse ornaments?

754
00:43:10.875 --> 00:43:12.667
They are stand-ins.

755
00:43:12.750 --> 00:43:14.208
What do you mean?

756
00:43:14.292 --> 00:43:19.750
We must have the <i>mononoke</i>
leave Lady Fuki's body.

757
00:43:21.542 --> 00:43:23.208
According to tradition,

758
00:43:23.292 --> 00:43:25.792
mice are considered
guardian deities of childbirth.

759
00:43:26.375 --> 00:43:27.208
Therefore,

760
00:43:27.292 --> 00:43:30.500
there are places where they must dwell.

761
00:43:30.583 --> 00:43:31.667
Wait!

762
00:43:31.750 --> 00:43:33.708
These won't burn, will they?

763
00:43:33.792 --> 00:43:36.375
I've only borrowed them, you know!

764
00:43:37.417 --> 00:43:41.083
Lady Fuki and Lady Suzu
may bear some similarities.

765
00:43:41.667 --> 00:43:43.083
Why do you think that?

766
00:43:43.167 --> 00:43:47.167
It would explain why
the <i>mononoke </i>is focused on her.

767
00:43:47.708 --> 00:43:51.625
Or perhaps explain why the Mother Hinezumi

768
00:43:51.708 --> 00:43:53.000
cannot be found.

769
00:43:55.542 --> 00:43:56.875
Now then.

770
00:44:19.542 --> 00:44:21.500
How are you feeling?

771
00:44:22.000 --> 00:44:25.292
Your father is waiting
in the grand chamber.

772
00:44:25.375 --> 00:44:26.375
Have a look.

773
00:44:26.875 --> 00:44:28.250
What do you think,

774
00:44:28.333 --> 00:44:29.792
Lady Suzu?

775
00:44:31.458 --> 00:44:33.375
How about that <i>uchikake</i>?

776
00:44:36.333 --> 00:44:39.167
Don't mind him, Lady Suzu.

777
00:44:39.250 --> 00:44:43.125
He's here as punishment
for fighting with a merchant.

778
00:44:43.625 --> 00:44:46.125
He's a rather hot-blooded man.

779
00:44:46.875 --> 00:44:48.417
You may raise your head.

780
00:44:49.083 --> 00:44:50.542
Sakashita?

781
00:44:51.792 --> 00:44:53.458
- What is it?
- Nothing.

782
00:44:54.292 --> 00:44:56.500
Take better care of your health.

783
00:45:00.917 --> 00:45:03.625
I'm sorry to have
kept you waiting, Father.

784
00:45:04.125 --> 00:45:06.292
What brings you here today?

785
00:45:07.583 --> 00:45:08.667
Suzu.

786
00:45:08.750 --> 00:45:10.792
Is something wrong?

787
00:45:11.292 --> 00:45:13.667
These days, the Saijo Family

788
00:45:13.750 --> 00:45:15.792
no longer worry about our next meal.

789
00:45:15.875 --> 00:45:17.208
It's all because of you…

790
00:45:17.292 --> 00:45:20.542
…and the favor His Majesty
has bestowed on you.

791
00:45:20.625 --> 00:45:22.292
R-Right.

792
00:45:22.375 --> 00:45:23.375
However…

793
00:45:23.458 --> 00:45:26.792
You were only able to enter the Ōoku…

794
00:45:26.875 --> 00:45:30.833
…because of Councilor Otomo's
introduction.

795
00:45:30.917 --> 00:45:34.875
I've never forgotten my debt
to Councilor Otomo.

796
00:45:34.958 --> 00:45:36.458
Councilor Otomo…

797
00:45:36.542 --> 00:45:38.167
…does not care for…

798
00:45:38.250 --> 00:45:39.667
…sparks that lead to conflict.

799
00:45:40.250 --> 00:45:41.500
Oh?

800
00:45:45.292 --> 00:45:48.458
- Your child is…
- …unwelcome.

801
00:45:50.208 --> 00:45:52.833
Councilor Otomo
has commanded me to abort the child?

802
00:45:53.333 --> 00:45:57.042
Councilor Otomo
would never say such a thing.

803
00:45:57.125 --> 00:45:58.917
Which is why we, his subordinates…

804
00:45:59.000 --> 00:46:00.708
…must act on our own

805
00:46:00.792 --> 00:46:03.542
to extinguish the sparks of conflict.

806
00:46:24.083 --> 00:46:25.583
Is this okay?

807
00:46:26.167 --> 00:46:28.750
I seem to have underestimated things.

808
00:46:41.250 --> 00:46:42.792
Is it over?

809
00:46:43.708 --> 00:46:44.750
No.

810
00:46:44.833 --> 00:46:46.000
Not yet.

811
00:46:46.500 --> 00:46:48.917
Sudo! Asanuma! Bring the burn ointment.

812
00:46:49.417 --> 00:46:50.250
Hurry!

813
00:46:50.333 --> 00:46:51.458
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

814
00:46:51.542 --> 00:46:54.583
These were merely Hinezumi children.

815
00:46:55.167 --> 00:46:56.583
Then there's more to come.

816
00:46:56.667 --> 00:46:58.208
The <i>mononoke</i>

817
00:46:58.708 --> 00:47:00.375
won't stop until it is slain.

818
00:47:01.458 --> 00:47:02.917
In order to draw your sword…

819
00:47:03.000 --> 00:47:04.917
I must locate Hinezumi's Reason.

820
00:47:05.000 --> 00:47:09.542
In other words,
the root of its urge to burn the Ōoku.

821
00:47:10.833 --> 00:47:12.708
Lady Fuki!

822
00:47:12.792 --> 00:47:14.458
Thank goodness.

823
00:47:23.917 --> 00:47:25.708
What is it, Saburomaru?

824
00:47:26.458 --> 00:47:28.833
A strange rumor has spread about Fuki.

825
00:47:29.333 --> 00:47:31.417
- You mean her pregnancy?
- No.

826
00:47:31.500 --> 00:47:35.458
They say she asked His Majesty
to make her the administrator of the Ōoku.

827
00:47:35.542 --> 00:47:38.167
<i>They found a letter
asking for his recommendation.</i>

828
00:47:40.792 --> 00:47:42.750
Fuki violated a taboo?

829
00:47:44.583 --> 00:47:45.833
Where did you find this?

830
00:47:45.917 --> 00:47:47.542
In the night chamber.

831
00:47:47.625 --> 00:47:50.458
Someone found it while cleaning.

832
00:47:51.208 --> 00:47:54.583
No one would dare
write a letter to His Majesty now.

833
00:47:54.667 --> 00:47:57.250
It was you who raised
the issue, Lady Botan.

834
00:47:57.792 --> 00:48:01.833
Correspondence or conversation
during night work is taboo, right?

835
00:48:02.917 --> 00:48:06.833
You seem to be going out of your way
to protect Lady Fuki.

836
00:48:07.458 --> 00:48:09.958
You allowed that strange man to enter,

837
00:48:10.042 --> 00:48:11.875
and now you even overlook the rules.

838
00:48:12.875 --> 00:48:16.167
It's remarkable
how kindhearted you've grown.

839
00:48:16.958 --> 00:48:18.750
As the administrator,

840
00:48:18.833 --> 00:48:20.917
the Ōoku is under my supervision.

841
00:48:21.500 --> 00:48:25.667
I'm merely showing concern
for Councilor Otomo's feelings.

842
00:48:26.167 --> 00:48:30.042
Aren't you the one
who's misunderstood, Lady Botan?

843
00:48:33.333 --> 00:48:35.750
That's all I have to say.

844
00:48:36.333 --> 00:48:39.208
I'll leave Lady Fuki's punishment to you.

845
00:48:40.833 --> 00:48:44.042
Lady Botan… the administrator.

846
00:48:48.417 --> 00:48:51.458
Your father will pay a visit soon.

847
00:48:54.833 --> 00:48:55.958
Father will?

848
00:48:57.667 --> 00:48:58.833
Lady Fuki.

849
00:48:58.917 --> 00:49:01.292
Do you have a moment?

850
00:49:03.667 --> 00:49:04.667
What is it?

851
00:49:04.750 --> 00:49:07.458
I believe you're aware

852
00:49:07.542 --> 00:49:11.583
that I served Lady Suzu long ago.

853
00:49:12.875 --> 00:49:13.875
Right.

854
00:49:14.375 --> 00:49:18.750
There's one thing
that I've never been able to forget.

855
00:49:19.417 --> 00:49:21.250
It's the way Lady Suzu looked

856
00:49:21.333 --> 00:49:24.458
on the day she perished in the fire.

857
00:49:26.333 --> 00:49:27.875
<i>Having lost her child,</i>

858
00:49:28.375 --> 00:49:31.333
<i>her face looked as if her soul</i>

859
00:49:31.417 --> 00:49:32.667
had been stripped away.

860
00:49:33.833 --> 00:49:35.292
At this moment, Lady Fuki,

861
00:49:36.667 --> 00:49:39.375
your face looks just like hers.

862
00:49:42.333 --> 00:49:46.167
Does this mean Lady Suzu
holds a grudge against the Ōoku?

863
00:49:46.667 --> 00:49:47.667
Her fire

864
00:49:47.708 --> 00:49:48.917
is cataclysmic.

865
00:49:49.000 --> 00:49:50.250
Cataclysmic?

866
00:49:50.333 --> 00:49:53.792
If we can find the Mother Hinezumi…

867
00:49:56.083 --> 00:49:57.083
Master Tokita!

868
00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:01.208
Sakashita.

869
00:50:01.708 --> 00:50:03.000
You know…

870
00:50:03.583 --> 00:50:04.583
What is it?

871
00:50:07.667 --> 00:50:09.333
Your brow has grown furrowed.

872
00:50:10.417 --> 00:50:11.417
What?

873
00:50:13.708 --> 00:50:15.833
You have something to tell me, right?

874
00:50:15.917 --> 00:50:16.958
Yes.

875
00:50:19.000 --> 00:50:20.000
Father?

876
00:50:21.000 --> 00:50:23.667
Councilor Otomo has summoned you.

877
00:50:26.000 --> 00:50:27.333
I will…

878
00:50:32.167 --> 00:50:33.083
Fuki…

879
00:50:33.167 --> 00:50:34.417
I've made my decision.

880
00:50:49.500 --> 00:50:51.333
I've been waiting for you.

881
00:50:52.125 --> 00:50:54.708
Father, what are they doing here?

882
00:50:55.917 --> 00:50:58.292
They happened to be in the area.

883
00:50:58.375 --> 00:50:59.500
Perfect timing.

884
00:50:59.583 --> 00:51:02.667
You have news
about Tokita's daughter, don't you?

885
00:51:03.750 --> 00:51:06.167
A letter was found yesterday.

886
00:51:06.958 --> 00:51:11.750
The letter asked His Majesty
to recommend a new administrator.

887
00:51:12.250 --> 00:51:14.708
It was signed by Lady Fuki.

888
00:51:15.792 --> 00:51:18.208
I heard everything from Katsunuma.

889
00:51:18.708 --> 00:51:20.542
It's a trap.

890
00:51:22.375 --> 00:51:24.292
A trap, you say?

891
00:51:24.375 --> 00:51:28.458
I believe it to be a forgery
designed to implicate Lady Fuki.

892
00:51:28.958 --> 00:51:31.708
Councilor Otomo, if I may speak…

893
00:51:31.792 --> 00:51:32.792
Shut up!

894
00:51:32.833 --> 00:51:34.708
What makes you think that?

895
00:51:34.792 --> 00:51:37.917
It's because Lady Fuki
is carrying a child.

896
00:51:39.000 --> 00:51:40.875
The Court Physician Gentaku

897
00:51:40.958 --> 00:51:42.958
tried to abort it using poison.

898
00:51:43.792 --> 00:51:45.417
The Matron who died earlier

899
00:51:46.083 --> 00:51:48.375
was attempting the same.

900
00:51:49.000 --> 00:51:51.167
Which means this sudden rumor too…

901
00:51:54.625 --> 00:51:56.500
And what's wrong with that?

902
00:52:06.167 --> 00:52:08.667
I fail to see the problem.

903
00:52:08.750 --> 00:52:11.958
A child who could become
the heir was nearly killed!

904
00:52:12.042 --> 00:52:13.250
The heir?

905
00:52:13.333 --> 00:52:15.708
That will never happen.

906
00:52:15.792 --> 00:52:17.292
But…

907
00:52:17.375 --> 00:52:18.500
Never!

908
00:52:34.208 --> 00:52:35.792
Much obliged.

909
00:52:36.375 --> 00:52:37.917
The Ōoku is in your hands.

910
00:52:40.125 --> 00:52:42.875
For generations, the mother of the heir

911
00:52:42.958 --> 00:52:45.250
has been from a councilor's family.

912
00:52:46.500 --> 00:52:48.250
A family without power of their own

913
00:52:48.333 --> 00:52:51.083
would only be used
by other ambitious lords,

914
00:52:51.167 --> 00:52:53.500
and the nation would plunge into chaos.

915
00:52:53.583 --> 00:52:56.417
But Father, you always told me
to protect the heir!

916
00:52:56.500 --> 00:52:58.833
An heir born to the Tokita Family

917
00:52:58.917 --> 00:53:01.375
would be the spark that sets Japan aflame.

918
00:53:01.458 --> 00:53:03.333
Extinguishing that spark

919
00:53:03.417 --> 00:53:04.708
is the righteous path.

920
00:53:10.792 --> 00:53:12.417
Did Lady Matsu really

921
00:53:13.250 --> 00:53:14.833
ask me to wait here?

922
00:53:17.708 --> 00:53:22.417
This realm needs those
who can see the bigger picture.

923
00:53:22.917 --> 00:53:27.375
Those who will take the initiative
and act for the Ōoku's sake.

924
00:53:27.875 --> 00:53:29.667
Tokita's daughter

925
00:53:29.750 --> 00:53:31.958
broke the rules of the Ōoku

926
00:53:32.042 --> 00:53:34.000
and passed a letter to His Majesty.

927
00:53:34.833 --> 00:53:36.375
Isn't that right, Botan?

928
00:53:36.458 --> 00:53:38.333
- Father!
- I command you!

929
00:53:38.417 --> 00:53:40.042
Defend the Ōoku!

930
00:53:40.625 --> 00:53:42.333
That is your duty!

931
00:53:42.417 --> 00:53:44.250
A witness discovered the letter.

932
00:53:44.333 --> 00:53:47.708
As the administrator, you must punish her.

933
00:53:47.792 --> 00:53:50.750
Is that too much to ask?

934
00:53:51.542 --> 00:53:54.083
How can you call that defending the Ōoku?

935
00:53:54.875 --> 00:53:58.625
The conspirators who did your bidding
have tarnished the Ōoku,

936
00:53:59.500 --> 00:54:01.958
and you are merely looking the other way!

937
00:54:03.708 --> 00:54:04.708
Fuki!

938
00:54:07.083 --> 00:54:08.833
Unforgivable!

939
00:54:18.375 --> 00:54:19.667
What's happening?

940
00:54:24.708 --> 00:54:25.708
Medicine Seller!

941
00:54:26.417 --> 00:54:27.417
Who let you in?!

942
00:54:28.667 --> 00:54:32.375
The passion of the concubine Suzu,
from 20 years ago, has become…

943
00:54:32.458 --> 00:54:34.000
- A <i>mononoke</i>!
- <i>Mononoke</i>?

944
00:54:34.083 --> 00:54:35.458
Hinezumi.

945
00:54:40.500 --> 00:54:42.250
Allow me to slay it.

946
00:54:44.833 --> 00:54:46.000
It burns!

947
00:54:46.083 --> 00:54:47.583
- What's happening?!
- Ow, ow!

948
00:54:47.667 --> 00:54:48.917
Down below?

949
00:54:50.708 --> 00:54:51.708
Huh?

950
00:55:02.167 --> 00:55:03.292
There you are.

951
00:55:16.417 --> 00:55:17.625
Matsu!

952
00:55:22.500 --> 00:55:23.625
Just how many lives

953
00:55:24.667 --> 00:55:26.583
have you people stolen?

954
00:55:26.667 --> 00:55:29.375
As the head of the Otomo Family,

955
00:55:29.458 --> 00:55:31.583
I've done everything for the Ōoku's sake!

956
00:55:33.792 --> 00:55:34.792
What is it doing?

957
00:55:37.667 --> 00:55:38.875
I don't know.

958
00:55:39.500 --> 00:55:42.333
But its voice is crying out,
"Unforgivable."

959
00:55:42.833 --> 00:55:43.708
What?

960
00:55:43.792 --> 00:55:47.250
Hinezumi burning itself is unheard of.

961
00:55:51.625 --> 00:55:55.750
Time and time again, I've extinguished
the sparks that could consume the nation!

962
00:55:55.833 --> 00:55:57.458
You'll never understand!

963
00:55:58.292 --> 00:56:01.708
Even so, you're the one
who forced Lady Suzu to abort her child!

964
00:56:03.458 --> 00:56:04.542
The Reason is at hand.

965
00:56:05.875 --> 00:56:07.542
I know nothing about any "Suzu"!

966
00:56:07.625 --> 00:56:09.500
I, myself, have never told anyone

967
00:56:09.583 --> 00:56:12.708
to abort their child!

968
00:56:13.583 --> 00:56:16.375
Hinezumi is crying out, "Unforgivable."

969
00:56:16.458 --> 00:56:17.750
Unforgivable?

970
00:56:18.250 --> 00:56:20.125
Loyal citizens merely took action

971
00:56:21.167 --> 00:56:23.250
to prevent conflict over succession!

972
00:56:28.625 --> 00:56:31.917
Hinezumi!
What is it that you can't forgive?

973
00:56:33.083 --> 00:56:35.125
Why do you consume yourself?

974
00:56:52.708 --> 00:56:53.833
Ow!

975
00:56:58.625 --> 00:57:00.167
<i>Unforgivable.</i>

976
00:57:01.750 --> 00:57:04.333
You want me to drink this?

977
00:57:04.417 --> 00:57:06.875
If I drink it, the Saijo Family

978
00:57:06.958 --> 00:57:09.500
will have served Councilor Otomo loyally.

979
00:57:09.583 --> 00:57:12.167
We can be proud of that, right?

980
00:57:12.250 --> 00:57:13.583
Suzu.

981
00:57:14.083 --> 00:57:15.250
Do you understand?

982
00:57:15.833 --> 00:57:17.667
I feel the same pain as you.

983
00:57:17.750 --> 00:57:20.917
No, even greater pain!

984
00:57:21.000 --> 00:57:23.458
I will protect the Saijo Family.

985
00:57:44.917 --> 00:57:46.167
Medicine Seller!

986
00:57:49.833 --> 00:57:51.000
It burns!

987
00:57:55.208 --> 00:57:56.958
Unforgivable…

988
00:58:06.833 --> 00:58:08.208
Unforgivable!

989
00:58:14.000 --> 00:58:17.708
It burns! Help, it burns!

990
00:58:19.250 --> 00:58:21.250
Botan! You must save me!

991
00:58:21.333 --> 00:58:24.042
If I die, what will become of the Ōoku?

992
00:58:24.125 --> 00:58:25.458
Or the nation itself?

993
00:58:25.542 --> 00:58:27.875
You aborted your own child.

994
00:58:28.917 --> 00:58:30.833
Rest assured, Father.

995
00:58:31.625 --> 00:58:35.625
And the regret consumed
your body in flames.

996
00:58:37.292 --> 00:58:40.000
Even if our lives end here,

997
00:58:40.583 --> 00:58:43.958
there are plenty of leaders
who could take our place!

998
00:58:44.042 --> 00:58:44.875
What?

999
00:58:44.958 --> 00:58:46.375
The one worthy of protection

1000
00:58:46.458 --> 00:58:48.667
is the child about to be born!

1001
00:59:00.292 --> 00:59:03.083
How could you let your child…

1002
00:59:06.375 --> 00:59:08.417
Is that Lady Suzu?

1003
00:59:10.208 --> 00:59:12.333
How could you let your child go?

1004
00:59:13.375 --> 00:59:14.250
Unforgivable!

1005
00:59:14.333 --> 00:59:15.333
I have…

1006
00:59:16.500 --> 00:59:18.333
- …done the…
- …done the…

1007
00:59:18.417 --> 00:59:19.417
…unforgivable.

1008
00:59:23.458 --> 00:59:25.625
"I have done the unforgivable."

1009
00:59:27.417 --> 00:59:30.292
So that's… how you felt.

1010
00:59:30.375 --> 00:59:31.500
The Reason…

1011
00:59:39.875 --> 00:59:41.375
Has been revealed!

1012
00:59:42.083 --> 00:59:45.375
Form, Truth, and Reason!

1013
00:59:47.875 --> 00:59:49.708
With these three elements in place,

1014
00:59:49.792 --> 00:59:52.375
I will release

1015
00:59:52.458 --> 00:59:53.583
my sword!

1016
00:59:53.667 --> 00:59:55.958
<i>Release!</i>

1017
01:01:14.792 --> 01:01:16.042
Hinezumi.

1018
01:01:16.542 --> 01:01:18.167
Even after becoming a <i>mononoke,</i>

1019
01:01:18.750 --> 01:01:22.667
your passion seeks to reduce you to ashes.

1020
01:01:26.542 --> 01:01:28.875
With the power of Kon,

1021
01:01:28.958 --> 01:01:31.500
one of the eight swords of Yin and Yang…

1022
01:01:34.083 --> 01:01:36.625
I shall purify you and lay you to rest.

1023
01:01:37.125 --> 01:01:38.500
<i>Mononoke.</i>

1024
01:01:38.583 --> 01:01:39.583
Go back!

1025
01:01:41.250 --> 01:01:42.375
Strike!

1026
01:01:58.500 --> 01:01:59.750
Forgive me.

1027
01:02:33.792 --> 01:02:34.917
I will give birth.

1028
01:02:35.583 --> 01:02:37.875
Whether the child is wanted or not.

1029
01:02:37.958 --> 01:02:40.333
I've made my decision.

1030
01:02:40.958 --> 01:02:44.500
I will inform Councilor Otomo myself.

1031
01:02:44.583 --> 01:02:45.708
But…

1032
01:02:45.792 --> 01:02:48.167
Fuki, at this rate,

1033
01:02:48.250 --> 01:02:50.167
your life will be in danger too.

1034
01:02:50.958 --> 01:02:51.958
I too

1035
01:02:52.625 --> 01:02:55.208
wish for the safety of my child.

1036
01:02:56.625 --> 01:02:58.125
You and I are the same.

1037
01:03:12.417 --> 01:03:14.458
- Lord Medicine Seller.
- Oh!

1038
01:03:14.542 --> 01:03:17.625
How can I ever thank you

1039
01:03:17.708 --> 01:03:19.250
for saving my sister?

1040
01:03:20.375 --> 01:03:23.208
I merely slew a <i>mononoke</i>.

1041
01:03:25.042 --> 01:03:27.917
By the way, what is all that luggage?

1042
01:03:28.000 --> 01:03:29.000
Oh, this?

1043
01:03:29.583 --> 01:03:32.583
Those are the same ornaments he burned!

1044
01:03:33.708 --> 01:03:35.750
I hope these can make up for it.

1045
01:03:36.250 --> 01:03:38.625
Everyone will be delighted!

1046
01:03:56.125 --> 01:04:00.625
You're willing to hand guardianship
of the child to us, the Fujimaki Family?

1047
01:04:00.708 --> 01:04:03.208
As the new chief councilor,

1048
01:04:03.708 --> 01:04:05.833
are you not in need of allies?

1049
01:04:06.333 --> 01:04:09.917
The Tokita Family shall be under my wing.

1050
01:04:10.417 --> 01:04:12.958
Now that Councilor Otomo has passed away,

1051
01:04:13.042 --> 01:04:16.458
Madam Suikoin has sole rule over the Ōoku.

1052
01:04:16.542 --> 01:04:19.917
<i>But if an heir were to be born…</i>

1053
01:04:20.000 --> 01:04:22.417
I do have one condition.

1054
01:04:23.417 --> 01:04:26.583
You want to raise
the child yourself, right?

1055
01:04:27.083 --> 01:04:29.750
I look forward to good news.

1056
01:04:30.250 --> 01:04:32.125
Master Sakashita!

1057
01:04:32.208 --> 01:04:35.542
Are you losing again?

1058
01:04:35.625 --> 01:04:36.542
What do you mean?

1059
01:04:36.625 --> 01:04:37.833
Just look!

1060
01:04:37.917 --> 01:04:40.042
He's got you cornered.

1061
01:04:40.125 --> 01:04:41.125
Huh?!

1062
01:04:43.333 --> 01:04:44.792
Good day, my lady.

1063
01:04:46.167 --> 01:04:47.917
- Good...
- Good day.

1064
01:04:50.708 --> 01:04:52.042
Good day.

1065
01:04:55.625 --> 01:04:57.250
Enough! I give up!

1066
01:04:57.333 --> 01:05:00.417
Shogi is boring anyway!

1067
01:05:00.500 --> 01:05:02.333
By the way, what are you doing here?

1068
01:05:02.417 --> 01:05:04.792
We'll be closing the gate soon.

1069
01:05:04.875 --> 01:05:07.958
Kume said she'd like to see the fireworks.

1070
01:05:08.583 --> 01:05:09.667
Fireworks?

1071
01:05:10.250 --> 01:05:13.917
I guess since
Councilor Otomo forbade them…

1072
01:05:14.417 --> 01:05:17.083
We're the fire patrol after all!

1073
01:05:17.583 --> 01:05:20.000
We have to monitor the fireworks too!

1074
01:05:20.083 --> 01:05:21.083
Ahem.

1075
01:05:22.250 --> 01:05:23.625
Lady Botan!

1076
01:05:25.917 --> 01:05:27.333
Are you all resting at once?

1077
01:05:27.417 --> 01:05:29.292
- No!
- We just…

1078
01:05:31.167 --> 01:05:32.708
Not too long, okay?

1079
01:05:32.792 --> 01:05:34.708
Please forgive… Wait, what?

1080
01:05:37.042 --> 01:05:39.833
Are you planning
to sneak into the Ōoku again?

1081
01:05:41.292 --> 01:05:43.583
Well, we'll see.

1082
01:05:47.292 --> 01:05:48.292
Let's pray…

1083
01:05:51.417 --> 01:05:53.500
You won't have to use this.

1084
01:06:20.750 --> 01:06:23.875
- Whoa, they're so pretty!
- Wow!

1085
01:06:24.583 --> 01:06:26.000
Amazing!

1086
01:06:33.625 --> 01:06:35.167
I will give birth.

1087
01:06:35.875 --> 01:06:36.875
So please…

1088
01:06:56.792 --> 01:06:58.333
This fire

1089
01:06:58.833 --> 01:06:59.833
is for mourning.

1090
01:07:16.042 --> 01:07:17.958
PART THREE

1091
01:07:18.042 --> 01:07:20.958
TO BE CONTINUED
IN "THE CURSE OF THE SERPENT"

1092
01:14:20.083 --> 01:14:23.333
THE ASHES OF RAGE

1093
01:14:23.417 --> 01:14:30.417
THE END

1094
01:14:31.000 --> 01:14:35.708
